    "body": "## Summary\r\nThis pull request adds subcommand support to the `cython` CLI while preserving full backward compatibility with the legacy command structure:\r\n- `cython MODULE.pyx` &rarr; `cython compile MODULE.pyx`\r\n- `cython --shared cyshared MODULE.pyx` &rarr; `cython compile --shared MODULE.pyx` (with `--shared` defaulting to `'cyshared'` if the name is omitted)\r\n- `cython --generate-shared cyshared.c` &rarr; `cython generate-shared cyshared.c`\r\n- `cythonize -fib MODULE.pyx` &rarr; `cython build -fi MODULE.pyx`\r\n\r\n## Subcommands Overview\r\n\r\n1. **`compile`**: Translates `.pyx` or `.py` files to C/C++. Supports all existing compiler options.\r\n2. **`generate-shared`**: Generates a shared C/C++ module with specified utility features (formerly `--generate-shared`).\r\n3. **`build`**: Compiles and builds extension modules using setuptools/distutils (acting as a clean alias for the `cythonize` CLI).\r\n\r\n## Key Implementation Details\r\n- **Backward Compatibility**: A custom argument preprocessing step checks if a subcommand was supplied. If not, it falls back to the legacy parser, ensuring existing build scripts and integrations do not break.\r\n- **`--shared` Defaulting**: Preprocesses `--shared` to default to `'cyshared'` if no value is explicitly supplied.\r\n- **Reusable Parsers**: Modified `Cythonize` argument parser to accept an `add_help` argument. This allows reusing the entire `cythonize` parser definition under the new `build` subcommand without option conflicts.\r\n- **Build Delegation**: If the `build` subcommand is detected, the CLI hands off control directly to `Cython.Build.Cythonize.main` and exits.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n- **`Cython/Build/Cythonize.py`**: Added `add_help` parameter to `create_args_parser` for subcommand parent parser support.\r\n- **`Cython/Compiler/CmdLine.py`**:\r\n  - Factored compile option additions into `add_compile_arguments`.\r\n  - Implemented `create_cython_subcommand_parser` with subparsers.\r\n  - Implemented `preprocess_shared_args` and subcommand detection logic.\r\n  - Updated `parse_command_line` to route subcommands/legacy configurations.\r\n- **`Cython/Compiler/Tests/TestCmdLine.py`**: Added comprehensive test coverage for `compile`, `generate-shared`, and `build` subcommands, as well as `--shared` defaulting.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\nRan the command-line parser test suite directly:\r\n```bash\r\npython -c \"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '.'); import unittest; import Cython.Compiler.Tests.TestCmdLine as t; unittest.main(t)\"\r\n```\r\nAll **56 unit tests passed successfully** (including existing legacy tests and the new subcommand/defaulting tests).\r\n",
